
<section class="phase-page">

    <h1>Test Planning</h1>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Project Overview</h2>
        <p>
            This project demonstrates manual software testing
            on the Automation Exercise e-commerce website.
            The goal is to verify selected user functionalities
            and document the testing process using a structured
            Quality Assurance approach.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Testing Objectives</h2>
        <ul class="goals-list">
            <li>Verify that selected website features work as expected.</li>
            <li>Test valid and invalid user inputs.</li>
            <li>Compare actual results with expected results.</li>
            <li>Document test cases and execution results.</li>
            <li>Identify and report defects when found.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Testing Scope</h2>

        <div class="cards-container">

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>User Registration</h3>
                <p>
                    Verify account creation and input validation
                    for registration fields.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>User Login</h3>
                <p>
                    Verify login functionality using valid
                    and invalid credentials.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Product Search</h3>
                <p>
                    Verify product search results using
                    different search inputs.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Shopping Cart</h3>
                <p>
                    Verify cart functionality, product quantities,
                    and displayed totals.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Testing Approach</h2>

        <div class="cards-container">

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Manual Testing</h3>
                <p>
                    Execute test cases manually from
                    the end-user perspective.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Black-Box Testing</h3>
                <p>
                    Verify system behavior without accessing
                    the application's source code.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Functional Testing</h3>
                <p>
                    Check whether selected features
                    behave according to expected results.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Testing Environment</h2>

        <ul class="goals-list">
            <li>Application: Automation Exercise</li>
            <li>Website: https://automationexercise.com</li>
            <li>Platform: Web Application</li>
            <li>Browser: Google Chrome</li>
            <li>Testing Method: Manual Testing</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="phase-section">
        <h2>Testing Tools & Deliverables</h2>

        <div class="cards-container">

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Microsoft Excel</h3>
                <p>
                    Used to document test cases,
                    expected results, and execution outcomes.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Jira</h3>
                <p>
                    Used to organize and track
                    testing activities and results.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="info-card">
                <h3>Test Evidence</h3>
                <p>
                    Screenshots collected to support
                    and document test execution.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </section>

</section>
